You are extracting enrollment+grade data from a Canvas LMS to identify at-risk students. Work ONLY with read-only Canvas tools and filesystem reads.

Process these 2 courses (course_id -> course_name):
- 1 -> "Applied Analytics & Algorithms (Fall 2013)"
- 2 -> "Applied Analytics & Algorithms (Fall 2014)"

For EACH course, do the following:
1. Pull ALL student enrollments and grades using mcp__canvas__canvas_get_course_grades(course_id, per_page=100, page=1,2,3,...). Keep paging until pagination.has_more is false. For each enrollment record, ONLY consider those where "type" == "StudentEnrollment". Record the current_score from the "grades" object — but ONLY if it is present and numeric (some enrollments have empty grades {} with no current_score; skip those). Build a list of (user_id, current_score).
2. Determine at-risk students: a student is at-risk in this course if current_score < 50.0. Classify risk_level: "Critical" if current_score < 40.0, else "Warning" if 40.0 <= current_score < 50.0.
3. Get student names: call mcp__canvas__canvas_list_course_users(course_id). This returns a large JSON array of users (id, name, ...). If the tool result is truncated (it may include an "output_path" pointing to a saved file in .tool_results), read the FULL content from that output_path using mcp__filesystem__read_text_file (the sub-agent shares the same workspace). Otherwise parse the returned JSON directly. Build a map user_id -> name.
4. Map each at-risk user_id to its name. Also compute the course summary: at_risk_count = number of at-risk students in that course; avg_score = arithmetic mean of current_score across ALL enrolled students (StudentEnrollment with a numeric current_score), rounded to 2 decimals.

OUTPUT FORMAT: Return ONLY a valid JSON object in exactly this shape:
{
  "at_risk": [
    {"student_name": "<name>", "course": "<course_name>", "current_score": <number>, "risk_level": "<Critical|Warning>"}
  ],
  "summary": [
    {"course": "<course_name>", "at_risk_count": <int>, "avg_score": <number>}
  ]
}
Put every at-risk student as one row in "at_risk" (they appear per course). Put one summary object per course. Do not add commentary outside the JSON. Round current_score and avg_score to 2 decimals.
Extract AAA course at-risk data

